Article 11
The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to: a. build a system for the implementation of protection for women and children, especially victims of violence, and their families;
b. provide facilities and infrastructure including safe houses/shelters, Human Resources comprising lawyers, doctors and psychologists-psychiatrists, volunteer companions, spiritual figures, economists, and social workers;
c. enhance the institutional capacity of protection providers, for victims of violence especially for women, children and their families; d. build a data and information center regarding protection, for victims of violence especially for women, children and their families; e. conduct monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection, for victims of violence especially for women, children and their families.

